---
import ClassificationBadge from '../components/ClassificationBadge.astro';
import ContentSection from '../components/ContentSection.astro';
import ContentPageLayout from '../layouts/ContentPageLayout.astro';
import CUTimeConverter from '../components/CUTimeConverter.astro';
---

<ContentPageLayout
  metaTitle="CU-Time | Cosmic Universalism"
  metaDescription="An introduction to CU-Time as a proposed deep-time coordinate system."
  eyebrow="CU-Time"
  title="A coordinate system for the Cosmic Breath"
  description="CU-Time is the framework’s proposed notation for locating dates and events within its deep-time model."
>
  <ContentSection
    id="cu-time-context"
    title="About this converter"
    variant="notice"
  >
    <p>
      CU-Time connects familiar chronology with the framework’s larger sequence of
      cosmic phases. The converter below translates between a proleptic Gregorian UTC
      date and a converter-aligned CU-Time value.
    </p>

    <p>
      This tool implements the documented mathematical constants and calendar rules.
      It does not generate phase classifications or empirical cosmology claims.
    </p>
  </ContentSection>

  <div class="cu-time-converter-breakout">
    <CUTimeConverter />
  </div>

  <div class="cu-time-details">
    <ContentSection id="cu-time-purpose-limits" title="Purpose and limits">
      <ClassificationBadge
        slot="context"
        classification="cu-mathematical-model"
      />

      <p>
        CU-Time is intended to provide consistent notation for positions within the
        Cosmic Breath framework. It is a CU-specific mathematical construction, and its
        usefulness depends on clearly documented definitions, assumptions, and conversion
        rules.
      </p>
    </ContentSection>

    <ContentSection id="cu-time-documentation" title="Conversion boundaries">
      <p>
        Gregorian inputs use explicit civil CE/BCE years and UTC. CU-Time inputs use plain
        decimal notation. The proleptic Gregorian calendar has no public civil year zero,
        and the original reference converter remains unchanged as historical evidence.
      </p>
    </ContentSection>

    <ContentSection id="cu-time-full-coordinate" title="CU-Time and the full Cosmic Breath coordinate">
      <p>
        CU-Time is the framework’s full Cosmic Breath coordinate, spanning from the sub-ZTOM seed boundary
        through the ZTOM reset boundary. The empirical Big Bang is an internal observable-universe reference
        within an already-existing CU-Time coordinate; it does not begin CU-Time, existence, or the Cosmic Breath.
      </p>
    </ContentSection>

    <ContentSection id="cu-time-observable-reference" title="The Observable-Universe Reference">
      <p>
        The Observable-Universe–Aligned CU Coordinate is a subordinate CU mathematical reference aligned with
        the converter’s adopted observable-universe age baseline. The derived age is not time elapsed since
        sub-ZTOM, and the coordinate-to-age ratio is a CU mathematical comparison rather than a standard
        empirical cosmology statistic.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Observable Universe marker appears between B-TOM and C-TOM because the governing CU Statement
        describes conscious existence as grounded on B-TOM and looking toward C-TOM. It is relational,
        non-selectable, not a TOM state, and not an empirical measurement.
      </p>
    </ContentSection>

    <ContentSection id="cu-time-precision" title="Method, precision, and uncertainty">
      <p>
        The converter uses deterministic Decimal arithmetic and documented calendar/model assumptions.
        Computational precision, calendar/model precision, and empirical uncertainty are distinct: long decimal
        results do not imply equivalent empirical certainty.
      </p>
    </ContentSection>
  </div>
</ContentPageLayout>

<style>
  .cu-time-converter-breakout {
    width: min(112rem, calc(100vw - clamp(2rem, 6vw, 6rem)));
    max-width: none;
    min-width: 0;
    margin-left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
  }

  .cu-time-details {
    display: grid;
    width: min(100%, 48rem);
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
    gap: var(--space-12);
  }
</style>
